<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SYNTHETIC SAMPLE — NO REAL TAXPAYER DATA. Written from scratch; all
  identities are deliberately fake, including the customs administration party
  (named "ÖRNEK GÜMRÜK İDARESİ" so it cannot be mistaken for a real one).

  BRANCH PROVED: EXPORT (IHRACAT / ISTISNA) — the single richest e-Fatura
  branch, and the one the plain-sale samples structurally cannot reach:

    · export.actualBuyer      — in IHRACAT the AccountingCustomerParty is the
                                CUSTOMS ADMINISTRATION; the real buyer sits in
                                cac:BuyerCustomerParty. Without this sample the
                                second party block is never rendered at all.
    · lineTable.gtip          — cac:GoodsItem/cbc:RequiredCustomsID
    · lineTable.packageType / packageNumber / packageCount
    · lineTable.deliveryPlace — line-level cac:DeliveryAddress
    · lineTable.despatchMode  — cac:ShipmentStage/cbc:TransportModeCode
    · lineTable.deliveryTerms — INCOTERMS
    · exemptionReason         — 0015 VAT is 0, so a written exemption reason is
                                mandatory (Schematron)

  The foreign buyer's own tax number lives in cac:PartyLegalEntity/cbc:CompanyID;
  the gate found that leaf MISSING once, so it is present here on purpose.
-->
